**v2 rename trap: `signIn` no longer exists.**

If you copy-paste from an older blog post or YouTube video you will likely see:

```ts
// OLD — v1 SDK, does not exist in v2
await supabase.auth.signIn({ email, password });
```

This silently fails (or throws `signIn is not a function`). The correct v2 call is:

```ts
// CORRECT — v2 SDK
const { data, error } = await supabase.auth.signInWithPassword({ email, password });
```

Same rule applies to the env variable: use `VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY`, not `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`, in Vite projects.
